---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon';
---

<Layout
  title="About us"
  description="More Than Mildly is a publication for curious minds: fresh perspectives, everyday discoveries, and room for a little wonder."
  ><div class="container">
    <div class="breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><span>About us</span>
    </div><section class="about-hero">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">A LITTLE ABOUT US</span><h1>
          Because mildly<br />interested is<br /><em>only the start.</em>
        </h1>
      </div><img
        class="editorial-image"
        src="/images/mountain-layers.jpg"
        alt="Layered rocky mountain peaks fade into haze beneath a pale sky."
        width="1000"
        height="1100"
      />
    </section><div class="about-content">
      <h2>There’s more to<br />look into.</h2><div class="prose">
        <p>
          More Than Mildly is a home for curious minds. We publish articles that
          explore the things people think about, care about, laugh about, and
          occasionally become a little obsessed with.
        </p><p>
          From the everyday to the unexpected, our categories are invitations to
          follow an interest. You might arrive for a fresh take on modern life
          and leave with a new question, a different perspective, or a small
          thing worth noticing.
        </p><h3>Room for a range of perspectives</h3><p>
          Our aim is to make thoughtful content comfortable to read and easy to
          explore, wherever you are in the world. Opinion belongs with context.
          Humour belongs with humanity. Curiosity belongs to everyone.
        </p><h3>How this publication is supported</h3><p>
          Advertising helps fund the publication. Ad placements are labelled,
          and paid promotional content should always be clearly identified. We
          don’t publish invented audience numbers or promise a particular
          campaign outcome.
        </p><a class="text-link" href="/advertise"
          >Build something interesting with us <Icon name="arrow" /></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div></Layout
>
